From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:25:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER (tools 0151): the keyword search reads 32 files at
 once (about 3x faster)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 1003: "你搜尋關鍵字 是用並列運算 去搜檔案嗎 怎感覺很慢"
- It was one file at a time: 4,364 files / 217 MB took 10-11 s here, nearly all
  of it waiting for the reads (decoding + matching all of them: 0.3 s).
- lib/projectsearch.js: pool(items, 32, fn, stop); search() reads 32 files at
  once, each file's hits in its own slot, joined in file order at the end -- the
  same list as before (checked on 4 searches against the old code: same hits,
  same order); limit / cancel still stop it. listFiles() lists a folder level at
  a time, its folders together. Now about 3 s.
- No in-memory cache: this PC has 7.7 GB with 1.5 GB free; keeping 217 MB of
  text resident is too much here.

Tests: run_all 3/3 layers (lib 183 -- a new one: 120 files in nested folders,
order / limit / cancel); real VS Code 156/159 (the 3 known stale checks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
